NimbyHands (display name Hands) is a fork of Give&Take.

Original work: Give&Take, Steam Workshop item 2903112334
  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2903112334
Author: affenb3rt (contact listed on the Workshop page as Discord)
Credited contributor (from the mod's config): Wardog
Original build: PBO version 23040119, packed with Mikero DePbo 8.07; Workshop last updated April 1, 2023.
Imported: October 14, 2026, from the copy recorded in
  logs/Copy-WorkshopItem-2903112334-20261014-153144.log
  (GiveAndTake.pbo sha256 EDBC6A285C15511CCF53FFFE2E3A3EF98C09759C00707B202496FF264C671574)

Permission: the original ships no license file. The Workshop description, read October 14, 2026,
grants permission to repack, reupload, modify, and redistribute the mod. The dated capture of that
text is PERMISSION.md in this folder; if the author changes the terms, re-check before the next
release.

Import notes:
- Scripts, inputs.xml, and languagecore/stringtable.csv are byte-for-byte copies.
- config.cpp is the original config.bin decoded to text; values are unchanged.
- logo.paa and Texheaders.bin were not imported; the NIMBY pack supplies its own mod presentation.

Players: the input actions were renamed on October 19, 2026. Anyone who changed the offer/request
key from O, or bound the pocket toggle, binds it once more under Options > Controls > NIMBY
("Hands: offer or request item", "Hands: open or close pockets").

Changes made for the NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp server are listed below, newest first.
- October 31, 2026 (NIMBY-T-063, the client-driven step 1, build 12):
  - A connected giver no longer receives a server-driven hand event. Submit sends NimbyHandsRpc.STAGE
    (6552101) to the giver's own client, which posts Man.PredictiveTakeToDst from hands into its own
    cargo (NimbyHandsClient), the move the inventory screen makes when a player drags the item in
    hands into cargo; the engine applies it on the server as any player-made move and signal 1
    writes STAGED as before. A client that cannot post the move answers STAGE_REFUSED (6552102) and
    the server writes REFUSED "client could not stage: <reason>"; silence is caught by the timeout.
    Ten server crashes on 1.30.164200 (October 28 to 30) each followed the server-driven hand event
    on a connected giver; the same step 2 with no hand event confirmed between two connected players
    (S6-D, October 31). A dummy giver (dev harness) keeps Man.ServerTakeToDst.
  - The build 10 CommandHandler plumbing (ModCommandHandlerBefore, OnCommandHandler, site=) stays in
    place for now; for a connected giver it only decides the frame the RPC is sent from.
- October 29, 2026, evening (NIMBY-T-063, crashes 4 to 8, the step 2 poll, step 2 without the giver):
  - While the step 2 move runs, every inventory signal handler returns at once and the end
    handler only notes that the signal fired; the CONFIRMED bookkeeping (registry, log, toast)
    runs after LocationSyncMoveEntity returns, outside the engine's callback. Crash 8 died inside
    that callback on a pure-script static call, after the move itself had put the item in the
    receiver's inventory.
  - Step 2 never touches the giver object. Seven crashes on 1.30.164200 died on the first
    operation inside the step 2 move that handed the stored giver reference to the engine or to
    a script call after the step 1 hand event (ServerTakeToDst, HasInventoryJuncture,
    GetIdentity), from the signal and from the poll alike, while the same reads on the giver in
    the step 2 validation passed moments earlier. The move runs LocationSyncMoveEntity and
    SendServerMove on the two locations only; Man.UpdateInventoryMenu is not called. The
    terminal toast resolves its two targets from GetGame().GetPlayers() by the identity ids
    captured at registration, so a player who left is not found rather than dereferenced.
  - Step 2 is no longer scheduled from inside the step 1 signal. Six server crashes on game
    build 1.30.164200 all ran step 2 from a CallLater posted inside EEItemLocationChanged (the
    engine's hand-event move) and died in the script VM on the first touch of the giver, at six
    different sites; every step 2 that confirmed (dev harness, the October 20 diagnostic) ran
    from a timer of its own. The dispatch now starts a 50 ms poll (NimbyHandsServer.Step2Tick,
    outside the callback) that runs step 2 for a STAGED transfer at least
    NimbyHandsConstants.STEP2_DELAY_MS (one tick) past the landing it recorded (stagedAtMs). The
    registry gained CollectByState for the poll. A 1000 ms delay from the signal was tried once
    (build 174154) and crashed the same way.
  - The juncture and reservation dumps write one debug line per native, so a crash in one of
    them leaves the values read before it (crash 4 lost the value HasInventoryJunctureItem had
    returned). The dispatch reads the giver's junctures before the hand event ("step 1
    junctures:"); step 2 names the giver through its identity ("step 2 giver:"), reads the
    reservations ("step 2 reservations:"), then runs the move natives, and no longer reads the
    junctures (crashes 4 and 5 died inside HasInventoryJuncture(giver, item)).
- October 29, 2026 (NIMBY-T-063, continued):
  - Step 2 runs the natives ServerTakeToDst would run, one at a time with a debug line after
    each (LocationSyncMoveEntity, SendServerMove, UpdateInventoryMenu), after a debug line that
    dumps the engine junctures and the script reservation on the item. Three server crashes in
    step 2 on October 28 left no script-side trace of which native died.
  - The terminal notification to the giver and the receiver is sent through the call queue,
    not from inside the state writer, which for CONFIRMED runs inside the engine's own move.
  - Dev harness switch: while NimbyHandsServer.AllowDummyParties(true) is on, a party with no
    identity passes the party check as connected, so the boot check can run a real transfer
    between two spawned dummies. Off by default; a connected player always has an identity.
  - NimbyHandsMoveItemToPlayer.Transfer() returns the registered request, so the dev harness can
    read a refusal after the wait tick (the registry evicts terminal entries).
- October 28, 2026 (NIMBY-T-063, the in-game run of October 28):
  - Step 1 is no longer dispatched from inside the action. The request is registered as PENDING,
    the server ends both players' offer and request loops, polls every 50 ms until both players
    are free, and dispatches then; a request still waiting at 3000 ms is refused as "giver
    inventory busy". The holder's hand state machine drops a hand event posted while the holder
    is inside an action command, which left every October 27 transfer UNCONFIRMED.
  - Step 2 runs one wait tick after the staged landing (was the same engine frame) and compares
    the item's location by type and parent entity only (no hierarchy walk, no cargo cell).
- October 21, 2026 (Hands plan v0.7, P3, ruling J2 of October 20 and the rulings of October 21):
  - A transfer is now two server moves under one id. Step 1 moves the item from the giver's
    hands into a free cargo location of the giver's own inventory (never a worn slot, never
    inside the item); its arrival is logged STAGED. Step 2, one tick later, revalidates and
    moves it from that exact location to the receiver's cargo with the synchronous server
    move and reads the result. A giver with no staging room is refused before step 1 and
    keeps the item in hands; a receiver who fills up between the steps leaves the item in
    the giver's cargo. Nothing is retried, cloned, restored, or deleted.
  - Every terminal outcome sends an on-screen notification to the giver and the receiver
    (NIMBY-T-012); a request refused before registration notifies the requester only.
  - All three verbs deliver into cargo only (was cargo or an attachment slot); Put In
    Pockets can no longer equip a worn slot on the receiver. The Put In Pockets prompt
    now also needs room in the receiver's cargo, and every prompt needs staging room in
    the giver's cargo.
  - The target condition's distance and must-be-alive arguments now reach CCTMan; the
    pocket toggle has a server-side 500 ms minimum interval per player (a repeat inside it
    is refused silently); location text names the owning player with both ids; a stale
    registry entry is reconciled before a request is refused as in flight; the offer and
    request loops mark the player dirty only when the state changes.
  - The reconcile at the 5-second timeout writes REFUSED when the item is still in the
    giver's inventory and UNCONFIRMED only when it is not. The self-test grew from 52 to
    156 cases.
- October 20, 2026 (test finding NIMBY-T-007): Data/Inputs.xml declares the sorting group "nimby"
  (label NIMBY) inside <inputs>, where 1.30 reads it; both Hands bindings now appear under a NIMBY tab
  in Options > Controls instead of Unsorted. No input names or defaults changed.
- October 19, 2026 (Hands plan Phase 2, decisions G1 and G2): renamed the addon from NimbyGiveTake
  to NimbyHands - folder, PBO, CfgPatches and CfgMods classes, every custom class and member
  (NimbyHands*), input actions (UANimbyOfferRequestItem to UANimbyHandsOfferRequest,
  UANimbyTogglePocketAccess to UANimbyHandsTogglePockets), string keys (STR_NIMBY_GT_* to
  STR_NIMBY_HANDS_*), log prefix ([NIMBY][GiveTake] to [NIMBY][Hands]), and profile folder
  ($profile:NimbyHands). inputs.xml moved to Data/Inputs.xml (sorted into the vanilla Others
  controls tab at the time, which 1.30 did not honor; see October 20): offer/request stays on O;
  the pocket toggle ships unbound with the label "Hands: open or close pockets" (the Left Shift + O combo also fired offer/request, test finding NIMBY-T-002).
  The two input labels are plain text now, so their string keys were removed. The pocket
  notification names the toggle's binding. Added PERMISSION.md for the Workshop permission text.
- October 19, 2026 (Hands plan Phase 1):
  - Every transfer is registered in a server-side in-flight registry with a correlation id before
    it is dispatched; a second request for an item already in flight is refused. Nothing is
    persisted.
  - Consent, both players' state (alive, conscious, not restrained, not in a vehicle, not
    swimming, still connected, not replaced), distance, the source item, the destination, and the
    engine's own move test are checked again immediately before dispatch.
  - The fixed one-second outcome check was replaced by lifecycle lines REQUESTED, CONFIRMED,
    REFUSED, and UNCONFIRMED, one terminal line per request: CONFIRMED comes from the item's
    location-change event on the server; a bounded 5-second timeout reconciles where the item is
    and never retries, clones, restores, or deletes anything.
  - Pockets (G4): the toggle cannot be used while restrained; the server closes open pockets on
    unconsciousness, restraint, reconnect, and respawn; Put In Pockets refuses an unconscious or
    restrained player. The toggle and every forced close write a pockets line.
  - Log lines carry both player ids (BI id and Steam64); names are quoted and escaped; debug
    lines appear only when $profile:<addon>\debug exists. A self-test runs when
    $profile:<addon>\selftest exists.
  - Removed the #ifdef DIAG blocks in the give and take actions, which set a state and never
    cleared it.
- October 14, 2026 (review CR-001): rewrote the transfer routine (NimbyMoveItemToPlayer). It now
  asks the player holding the item to move it with the vanilla server path (ServerTakeToDst), which
  runs through that player's own hand state machine, instead of deleting the item's network state
  and injecting fake hand events on both players. Transfers land in the receiver's inventory
  (cargo or an attachment slot), never their hands; Give now delivers to inventory and the
  "take to hands" action was removed. Each transfer logs REQUESTED, then OK or FAILED once the
  receiver has checked where the item ended up.
- October 14, 2026 (review CR-005, CR-006, CR-003):
  - Renamed every class, input action, string key, and member with a Nimby prefix so the fork
    cannot collide with the original or another mod; fixed misspellings (Pocktes, Toggel, Cancle)
    and renamed the two misspelled script files. The modded GameConstants member became
    NimbyGiveTakeConstants. Addon, CfgMods class, and PBO prefix are now NimbyGiveTake.
  - Every transfer now writes one [NIMBY][GiveTake] line to the server script log naming the
    action, result, giver, receiver, and item. Expected refusals (no item, no space, item already
    taken) are logged there instead of raising Error() with no context.
  - The pocket-access toggle, unbound in the original, defaults to Left Shift + O.
- October 14, 2026: removed the four CfgMods picture and logo entries that point at logo.paa,
  which is not imported. Without this, the game logs a missing-file error for the image.
